<section id="Ax1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix">Appendix</h2>

<div id="Ax1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Multiple intermediary results are necessary in order to prove <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ 2.5 Main identifiability result ‣ 2 Identifiability analysis of LAPO ‣ On the Identifiability of Latent Action Policies" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. The proof of the following technical lemma can be safely skipped at first read.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 2</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> be a metric space<span id="footnote4" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">4</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">4</sup>
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note"><span id="footnote4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">4</span></span>
                
                
                
                
                
                
                
              <span id="footnote4.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">The result generalizes to the case where </span><math id="footnote4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math><span id="footnote4.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright"> is a perfectly normal topological space.</span></span></span></span> and let <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{1},X_{2},...,X_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{1},X_{2},...,X_{K}</annotation></semantics></math> be a finite collection of disjoint closed sets of <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, there exists a function <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q:[K]\times X\rightarrow[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q:[K]\times X\rightarrow[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<ul id="Ax1.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="Ax1.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ax1.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax1.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">for all </span><math id="Ax1.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in X</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Ax1.I2.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, </span><math id="Ax1.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k\in[K]}q(k\mid x)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k\in[K]}q(k\mid x)=1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Ax1.I2.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">,</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ax1.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ax1.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax1.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">for all </span><math id="Ax1.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in[K]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in[K]</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Ax1.I2.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, </span><math id="Ax1.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(k\mid x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(k\mid x)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Ax1.I2.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is continuous in </span><math id="Ax1.I2.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Ax1.I2.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> (as a function </span><math id="Ax1.I2.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\rightarrow[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\rightarrow[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Ax1.I2.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">), and</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ax1.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ax1.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax1.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">for all </span><math id="Ax1.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in[K]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in[K]</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Ax1.I2.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and all </span><math id="Ax1.I2.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in X_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in X_{k}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Ax1.I2.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, </span><math id="Ax1.I2.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(k\mid x)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(k\mid x)=1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Ax1.I2.i3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Ax1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="Ax1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">We make use of the Vedenissoff theorem <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>, Theorem 1.5.19]</cite>. We extract only the part of the theorem we will need: If a topological space <math id="Ax1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> is perfectly normal, then for every pair of disjoint closed sets <math id="Ax1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A,B\subseteq X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A,B\subseteq X</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists a continuous function <math id="Ax1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:X\rightarrow[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:X\rightarrow[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="Ax1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{-1}(\{0\})=A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{-1}(\{0\})=A</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Ax1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{-1}(\{1\})=B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{-1}(\{1\})=B</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Ax1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since a metric space is always perfectly normal <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>, Corollary 4.1.13]</cite>, <math id="Ax1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> is perfectly normal and thus we can apply the Vedenissoff theorem.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Ax1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">For each <math id="Ax1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in[K]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in[K]</annotation></semantics></math>, the set <math id="Ax1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigcup_{k^{\prime}\in[K]\setminus\{k\}}X_{k^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>⋃</mo><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><msub><mi>X</mi><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigcup_{k^{\prime}\in[K]\setminus\{k\}}X_{k^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> is closed since a finite union of closed sets is closed. By Vedenissoff theorem, there exists a continuous function <math id="Ax1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{k}:X\rightarrow[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{k}:X\rightarrow[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="Ax1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{k}^{-1}(\{1\})=X_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{k}^{-1}(\{1\})=X_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Ax1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{k}^{-1}(\{0\})=\bigcup_{k^{\prime}\in[K]\setminus\{k\}}X_{k^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>⋃</mo><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><msub><mi>X</mi><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{k}^{-1}(\{0\})=\bigcup_{k^{\prime}\in[K]\setminus\{k\}}X_{k^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Ax1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">We now prove that <math id="Ax1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k\in[K]}h_{k}(x)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k\in[K]}h_{k}(x)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="Ax1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in X</annotation></semantics></math>. We consider two cases, <math id="Ax1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\bigcup_{k\in[K]}X_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">∈</mo><mrow><msub><mo>⋃</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\bigcup_{k\in[K]}X_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Ax1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\not\in\bigcup_{k\in[K]}X_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">∉</mo><mrow><msub><mo>⋃</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\not\in\bigcup_{k\in[K]}X_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="Ax1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\bigcup_{k\in[K]}X_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">∈</mo><mrow><msub><mo>⋃</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\bigcup_{k\in[K]}X_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, then there exists a <math id="Ax1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{0}\in[K]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{0}\in[K]</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="Ax1.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in X_{k_{0}}=h_{k_{0}}^{-1}(\{1\})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in X_{k_{0}}=h_{k_{0}}^{-1}(\{1\})</annotation></semantics></math> which means <math id="Ax1.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{k_{0}}(x)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{k_{0}}(x)=1</annotation></semantics></math>. Of course, this implies that the sum is greater than zero. If <math id="Ax1.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\not\in\bigcup_{k\in[K]}X_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">∉</mo><mrow><msub><mo>⋃</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\not\in\bigcup_{k\in[K]}X_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, in particular we have <math id="Ax1.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\not\in\bigcup_{k\in[K]\setminus\{1\}}X_{k}=h_{1}^{-1}(\{0\})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">∉</mo><mrow><msub><mo>⋃</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\not\in\bigcup_{k\in[K]\setminus\{1\}}X_{k}=h_{1}^{-1}(\{0\})</annotation></semantics></math>, which means <math id="Ax1.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{1}(x)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{1}(x)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Of course, this implies the sum is greater than zero.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Ax1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="Ax1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k\in[K]}h_{k}(x)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k\in[K]}h_{k}(x)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="Ax1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in X</annotation></semantics></math>, we can define, for all <math id="Ax1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(k,x)\in[K]\times X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(k,x)\in[K]\times X</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="Ax1.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ax1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(k\mid x):=\frac{h_{k}(x)}{\sum_{{k^{\prime}}\in[K]}h_{k^{\prime}}(x)}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(k\mid x):=\frac{h_{k}(x)}{\sum_{{k^{\prime}}\in[K]}h_{k^{\prime}}(x)}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Ax1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">We now verify that <math id="Ax1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the three conditions of the theorem. First, it is clear that <math id="Ax1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k\in[K]}q(k\mid x)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k\in[K]}q(k\mid x)=1</annotation></semantics></math>. Second, <math id="Ax1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(k\mid x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(k\mid x)</annotation></semantics></math> is continuous in <math id="Ax1.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> since all <math id="Ax1.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{k^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{k^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> are continuous functions.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Ax1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Third, we check that <math id="Ax1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(k\mid x)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(k\mid x)=1</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="Ax1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in X_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in X_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="Ax1.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in[K]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in[K]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Ax1.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in X_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in X_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="Ax1.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{k}=h^{-1}_{k}(\{1\})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{k}=h^{-1}_{k}(\{1\})</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that <math id="Ax1.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{k}(x)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{k}(x)=1</annotation></semantics></math>. Consider <math id="Ax1.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k^{\prime}\in[K]\setminus\{k\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k^{\prime}\in[K]\setminus\{k\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Clearly, <math id="Ax1.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in X_{k}\subseteq\bigcup_{k^{\prime\prime}\in[K]\setminus\{k^{\prime}\}}X_{k^{\prime\prime}}=h^{-1}_{k^{\prime}}(\{0\})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">⊆</mo><mrow><msub><mo>⋃</mo><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><msub><mi>X</mi><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in X_{k}\subseteq\bigcup_{k^{\prime\prime}\in[K]\setminus\{k^{\prime}\}}X_{k^{\prime\prime}}=h^{-1}_{k^{\prime}}(\{0\})</annotation></semantics></math>, which means <math id="Ax1.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{k^{\prime}}(x)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{k^{\prime}}(x)=0</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="Ax1.p8.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k^{\prime}\not=k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k^{\prime}\not=k</annotation></semantics></math>. We thus have</span></p>
<table id="Ax1.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ax1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(k\mid x)=\frac{h_{k}(x)}{h_{k}(x)+\sum_{{k^{\prime}}\in[K]\setminus\{k\}}h_{k^{\prime}}(x)}=\frac{1}{1+0}=1\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(k\mid x)=\frac{h_{k}(x)}{h_{k}(x)+\sum_{{k^{\prime}}\in[K]\setminus\{k\}}h_{k^{\prime}}(x)}=\frac{1}{1+0}=1\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ax1.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax1.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">which concludes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Ax1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.p9.1" class="ltx_p">Define the function <math id="Ax1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G:{\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{A}}\rightarrow{\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{X}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G:{\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{A}}\rightarrow{\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{X}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="Ax1.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G({\bm{x}},a):=({\bm{x}},{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝒈</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G({\bm{x}},a):=({\bm{x}},{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a))</annotation></semantics></math>, which is simply the function <math id="Ax1.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒈</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a)</annotation></semantics></math> with a copy of <math id="Ax1.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒙</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> in its output. Note that its image <math id="Ax1.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G({\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{A}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G({\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{A}})</annotation></semantics></math> is effectively the set of plausible transition pairs <math id="Ax1.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>. In general, this is expected to be a proper subset of <math id="Ax1.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{X}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{X}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under <a href="#Thmassumption2" title="Assumption 2 (Injectivity). ‣ 2.5 Main identifiability result ‣ 2 Identifiability analysis of LAPO ‣ On the Identifiability of Latent Action Policies" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Assumption</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> is injective.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Ax1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="Ax1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax1.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">If <math id="Ax1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G({\bm{x}}_{1},{\bm{a}}_{1})=G({\bm{x}}_{2},{\bm{a}}_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G({\bm{x}}_{1},{\bm{a}}_{1})=G({\bm{x}}_{2},{\bm{a}}_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="Ax1.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{1}={\bm{x}}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{1}={\bm{x}}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Ax1.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}}_{1},a_{1})={\bm{g}}({\bm{x}}_{1},a_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒈</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝒈</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}}_{1},a_{1})={\bm{g}}({\bm{x}}_{1},a_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> and thus, by <a href="#Thmassumption2" title="Assumption 2 (Injectivity). ‣ 2.5 Main identifiability result ‣ 2 Identifiability analysis of LAPO ‣ On the Identifiability of Latent Action Policies" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Assumption</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, <math id="Ax1.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{1}=a_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1}=a_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmremark2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmremark2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 2</span></span><span id="Thmremark2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmremark2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmremark2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmremark2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Since <math id="Thmremark2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> is injective, it is bijective on its image <math id="Thmremark2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G({\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{A}})\subseteq{\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{X}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G({\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{A}})\subseteq{\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{X}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, it has an inverse <math id="Thmremark2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F:G({\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{A}})\rightarrow{\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F:G({\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{A}})\rightarrow{\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{A}}</annotation></semantics></math> which clearly has the form <math id="Thmremark2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F({\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})=({\bm{x}},{\bm{f}}({\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F({\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})=({\bm{x}},{\bm{f}}({\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime}))</annotation></semantics></math>, for some function <math id="Thmremark2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{f}}:G({\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{A}})\rightarrow{\mathcal{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐟</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{f}}:G({\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{A}})\rightarrow{\mathcal{A}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 4</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1 (Continuous 𝒈). ‣ 2.5 Main identifiability result ‣ 2 Identifiability analysis of LAPO ‣ On the Identifiability of Latent Action Policies" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Assumptions</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and <a href="#Thmassumption2" title="Assumption 2 (Injectivity). ‣ 2.5 Main identifiability result ‣ 2 Identifiability analysis of LAPO ‣ On the Identifiability of Latent Action Policies" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> hold and <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{k}\geq k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>≥</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{k}\geq k</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, there exist <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{g}}^{*}\in{\mathcal{G}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐠</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{g}}^{*}\in{\mathcal{G}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{*}\in{\mathcal{Q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{*}\in{\mathcal{Q}}</annotation></semantics></math> such that the objective of Problem <a href="#S2.E1" title="In 2.3 A formal entropy-regularized LAPO objective ‣ 2 Identifiability analysis of LAPO ‣ On the Identifiability of Latent Action Policies" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> is equal to zero.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Ax1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="Ax1.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax1.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">Take <math id="Ax1.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{g}}^{*}({\bm{x}},\hat{a}):=\mathbf{1}(\hat{a}\in{\mathcal{A}}){\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},\hat{a})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝒈</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒈</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{g}}^{*}({\bm{x}},\hat{a}):=\mathbf{1}(\hat{a}\in{\mathcal{A}}){\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},\hat{a})</annotation></semantics></math>. Essentially, <math id="Ax1.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{g}}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒈</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{g}}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> imitates the ground-truth FDM <math id="Ax1.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{g}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒈</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{g}}</annotation></semantics></math> when the action <math id="Ax1.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{a}\in{\mathcal{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{a}\in{\mathcal{A}}</annotation></semantics></math>, otherwise it simply outputs zero. Clearly, <math id="Ax1.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{g}}^{*}\in{\mathcal{G}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝒈</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{g}}^{*}\in{\mathcal{G}}</annotation></semantics></math> since, by <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1 (Continuous 𝒈). ‣ 2.5 Main identifiability result ‣ 2 Identifiability analysis of LAPO ‣ On the Identifiability of Latent Action Policies" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Assumption</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, <math id="Ax1.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{g}}(\cdot,\hat{a})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒈</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{g}}(\cdot,\hat{a})</annotation></semantics></math> is continuous for all <math id="Ax1.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{a}\in{\mathcal{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{a}\in{\mathcal{A}}</annotation></semantics></math> (and the zero function is continuous).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Ax1.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax1.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">We now construct a <math id="Ax1.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{*}\in{\mathcal{Q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{*}\in{\mathcal{Q}}</annotation></semantics></math> such that, for all <math id="Ax1.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})\in G({\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{A}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})\in G({\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{A}})</annotation></semantics></math> and all <math id="Ax1.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{a}\in\hat{\mathcal{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{a}\in\hat{\mathcal{A}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="Ax1.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{*}(\hat{a}\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})=\delta({\bm{f}}({\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})-\hat{a})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒇</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{*}(\hat{a}\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})=\delta({\bm{f}}({\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})-\hat{a})</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="Ax1.p12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{f}}({\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒇</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{f}}({\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> is defined in <a href="#Thmremark2" title="Remark 2. ‣ Appendix ‣ On the Identifiability of Latent Action Policies" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Remark</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. Later on, we show that the pair <math id="Ax1.p12.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(q^{*},{\bm{g}}^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒈</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(q^{*},{\bm{g}}^{*})</annotation></semantics></math> sets the objective to zero.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Ax1.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax1.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">Notice that <math id="Ax1.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G({\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{A}})=\bigcup_{a\in{\mathcal{A}}}G({\mathcal{X}}\times\{a\})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>⋃</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G({\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{A}})=\bigcup_{a\in{\mathcal{A}}}G({\mathcal{X}}\times\{a\})</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="Ax1.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G({\mathcal{X}}\times\{a\})=\{({\bm{x}},{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a))\mid{\bm{x}}\in{\mathcal{X}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝒈</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G({\mathcal{X}}\times\{a\})=\{({\bm{x}},{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a))\mid{\bm{x}}\in{\mathcal{X}}\}</annotation></semantics></math> is the graph of <math id="Ax1.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{g}}(\cdot,a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒈</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{g}}(\cdot,a)</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="Ax1.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{g}}(\cdot,a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒈</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{g}}(\cdot,a)</annotation></semantics></math> is continuous by <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1 (Continuous 𝒈). ‣ 2.5 Main identifiability result ‣ 2 Identifiability analysis of LAPO ‣ On the Identifiability of Latent Action Policies" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Assumption</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, the closed graph theorem implies that its graph, <math id="Ax1.p13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G({\mathcal{X}}\times\{a\})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G({\mathcal{X}}\times\{a\})</annotation></semantics></math>, is closed is <math id="Ax1.p13.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{X}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{X}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. Furthermore, we know that the sets <math id="Ax1.p13.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G({\mathcal{X}}\times\{a\})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G({\mathcal{X}}\times\{a\})</annotation></semantics></math> are mutually disjoint since otherwise there exists <math id="Ax1.p13.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})\in G({\mathcal{X}}\times\{a_{1}\})\cap G({\mathcal{X}}\times\{a_{2}\})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})\in G({\mathcal{X}}\times\{a_{1}\})\cap G({\mathcal{X}}\times\{a_{2}\})</annotation></semantics></math> for distinct <math id="Ax1.p13.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Ax1.p13.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> which implies <math id="Ax1.p13.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\bm{x}},{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a_{1}))=({\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})=({\bm{x}},{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a_{2}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝒈</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝒈</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\bm{x}},{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a_{1}))=({\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})=({\bm{x}},{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a_{2}))</annotation></semantics></math>, which violates <a href="#Thmassumption2" title="Assumption 2 (Injectivity). ‣ 2.5 Main identifiability result ‣ 2 Identifiability analysis of LAPO ‣ On the Identifiability of Latent Action Policies" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Assumption</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Ax1.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax1.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">To summarize, the last paragraph showed that <math id="Ax1.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{G({\mathcal{X}}\times\{a\})\}_{a\in{\mathcal{A}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{G({\mathcal{X}}\times\{a\})\}_{a\in{\mathcal{A}}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a partition of <math id="Ax1.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G({\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{A}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G({\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{A}})</annotation></semantics></math> where each <math id="Ax1.p14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G({\mathcal{X}}\times\{a\})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G({\mathcal{X}}\times\{a\})</annotation></semantics></math> is closed in <math id="Ax1.p14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{X}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{X}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. By noticing that <math id="Ax1.p14.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{X}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{X}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is a metric space, we can apply <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma 2. ‣ Appendix ‣ On the Identifiability of Latent Action Policies" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> to show the existence of a function <math id="Ax1.p14.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q:{\mathcal{A}}\times{\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{X}}^{\prime}\rightarrow[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q:{\mathcal{A}}\times{\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{X}}^{\prime}\rightarrow[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> such that the following holds:</span></p>
<ul id="Ax1.I3" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="Ax1.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ax1.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">for all <math id="Ax1.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})\in{\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{X}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})\in{\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{X}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Ax1.I3.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{a\in{\mathcal{A}}}q(a\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{a\in{\mathcal{A}}}q(a\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})=1</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ax1.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ax1.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">for all <math id="Ax1.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in{\mathcal{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in{\mathcal{A}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Ax1.I3.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(a\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(a\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> is continuous in <math id="Ax1.I3.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>, and</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ax1.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ax1.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">for all <math id="Ax1.I3.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in{\mathcal{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in{\mathcal{A}}</annotation></semantics></math> and all <math id="Ax1.I3.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})\in G({\mathcal{X}}\times\{a\})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})\in G({\mathcal{X}}\times\{a\})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Ax1.I3.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(a\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(a\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})=1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="Ax1.p14.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax1.p14.2.1" class="ltx_text">We choose, for all <math id="Ax1.p14.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\hat{a},{\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})\in\hat{\mathcal{A}}\times{\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{X}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\hat{a},{\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})\in\hat{\mathcal{A}}\times{\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{X}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Ax1.p14.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{*}(\hat{a}\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime}):=\mathbf{1}(\hat{a}\in{\mathcal{A}})q(\hat{a}\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{*}(\hat{a}\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime}):=\mathbf{1}(\hat{a}\in{\mathcal{A}})q(\hat{a}\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>. In other words, <math id="Ax1.p14.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> imitates <math id="Ax1.p14.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="Ax1.p14.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{a}\in{\mathcal{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{a}\in{\mathcal{A}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and simply outputs zero when <math id="Ax1.p14.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{a}\not\in{\mathcal{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∉</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{a}\not\in{\mathcal{A}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Ax1.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax1.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">We now check that <math id="Ax1.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{*}\in{\mathcal{Q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{*}\in{\mathcal{Q}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Take <math id="Ax1.p15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})\in{\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{X}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})\in{\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{X}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. We have</span></p>
<table id="Ax1.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Ax1.E2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ax1.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{\hat{a}\in\hat{\mathcal{A}}}q^{*}(\hat{a}\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})=\sum_{\hat{a}\in\hat{\mathcal{A}}}\mathbf{1}(\hat{a}\in{\mathcal{A}})q(\hat{a}\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})=\sum_{\hat{a}\in{\mathcal{A}}}q(\hat{a}\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})=1\,.\," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{\hat{a}\in\hat{\mathcal{A}}}q^{*}(\hat{a}\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})=\sum_{\hat{a}\in\hat{\mathcal{A}}}\mathbf{1}(\hat{a}\in{\mathcal{A}})q(\hat{a}\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})=\sum_{\hat{a}\in{\mathcal{A}}}q(\hat{a}\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})=1\,.\,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ax1.p15.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax1.p15.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the second equality used the fact that <math id="Ax1.p15.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{A}}\subseteq\hat{\mathcal{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{A}}\subseteq\hat{\mathcal{A}}</annotation></semantics></math> (since <math id="Ax1.p15.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{k}\geq k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>≥</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{k}\geq k</annotation></semantics></math>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Ax1.p16" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax1.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now take <math id="Ax1.p16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{a}\in\hat{\mathcal{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{a}\in\hat{\mathcal{A}}</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="Ax1.p16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{a}\in{\mathcal{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{a}\in{\mathcal{A}}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="Ax1.p16.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{*}(\hat{a}\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})=q(a\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{*}(\hat{a}\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})=q(a\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> which is continuous in <math id="Ax1.p16.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="Ax1.p16.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{a}\not\in{\mathcal{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∉</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{a}\not\in{\mathcal{A}}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="Ax1.p16.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{*}(\hat{a}\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{*}(\hat{a}\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})=0</annotation></semantics></math> which is also continuous. Thus <math id="Ax1.p16.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{*}\in{\mathcal{Q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{*}\in{\mathcal{Q}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Ax1.p17" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.p17.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax1.p17.1.1" class="ltx_text">Notice that, for all <math id="Ax1.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\bm{x}},a)\in{\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\bm{x}},a)\in{\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{A}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="Ax1.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Ax1.E3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ax1.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q^{*}(\hat{a}\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a))=\mathbf{1}(\hat{a}\in{\mathcal{A}})q(\hat{a}\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a))=\mathbf{1}(\hat{a}\in{\mathcal{A}})\mathbf{1}(\hat{a}=a)=\mathbf{1}(\hat{a}=a)\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝒈</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝒈</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q^{*}(\hat{a}\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a))=\mathbf{1}(\hat{a}\in{\mathcal{A}})q(\hat{a}\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a))=\mathbf{1}(\hat{a}\in{\mathcal{A}})\mathbf{1}(\hat{a}=a)=\mathbf{1}(\hat{a}=a)\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ax1.p17.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax1.p17.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the third equality holds because <math id="Ax1.p17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\bm{x}},{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a))\in G({\mathcal{X}}\times\{a\})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝒈</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\bm{x}},{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a))\in G({\mathcal{X}}\times\{a\})</annotation></semantics></math>, which implies that <math id="Ax1.p17.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{q(a\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a))=1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝒈</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{q(a\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a))=1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Ax1.p18" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.p18.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax1.p18.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now, we must show that the pair <math id="Ax1.p18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\bm{g}}^{*},q^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒈</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\bm{g}}^{*},q^{*})</annotation></semantics></math> sets the loss of Problem <a href="#S2.E1" title="In 2.3 A formal entropy-regularized LAPO objective ‣ 2 Identifiability analysis of LAPO ‣ On the Identifiability of Latent Action Policies" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> to zero. First note that</span></p>
<table id="Ax1.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Ax1.E4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ax1.E4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathbb{E}}_{p({\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})}H(q^{*}(\cdot\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathbb{E}}_{p({\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})}H(q^{*}(\cdot\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ax1.E4.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle={\mathbb{E}}_{p({\bm{x}},a)}H(q^{*}(\cdot\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a)))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒈</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle={\mathbb{E}}_{p({\bm{x}},a)}H(q^{*}(\cdot\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a)))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ax1.E5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ax1.E5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle={\mathbb{E}}_{p({\bm{x}},a)}H(\mathbf{1}(\cdot=a))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle={\mathbb{E}}_{p({\bm{x}},a)}H(\mathbf{1}(\cdot=a))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ax1.E6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ax1.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle={\mathbb{E}}_{p({\bm{x}},a)}0=0\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle={\mathbb{E}}_{p({\bm{x}},a)}0=0\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Ax1.p19" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.p19.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax1.p19.1.1" class="ltx_text">Also,</span></p>
<table id="Ax1.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Ax1.E7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ax1.E7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathbb{E}}_{p({\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})}\sum_{\hat{a}\in\hat{\mathcal{A}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathbb{E}}_{p({\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})}\sum_{\hat{a}\in\hat{\mathcal{A}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ax1.E7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q^{*}(\hat{a}\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})\lVert{\bm{x}}^{\prime}-{\bm{g}}^{*}({\bm{x}},\hat{a})\rVert^{2}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒈</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q^{*}(\hat{a}\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})\lVert{\bm{x}}^{\prime}-{\bm{g}}^{*}({\bm{x}},\hat{a})\rVert^{2}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ax1.E8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ax1.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle={\mathbb{E}}_{p({\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})}\sum_{\hat{a}\in\hat{\mathcal{A}}}q^{*}(\hat{a}\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})\lVert{\bm{x}}^{\prime}-\mathbf{1}(\hat{a}\in{\mathcal{A}}){\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},\hat{a})\rVert^{2}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒈</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle={\mathbb{E}}_{p({\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})}\sum_{\hat{a}\in\hat{\mathcal{A}}}q^{*}(\hat{a}\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})\lVert{\bm{x}}^{\prime}-\mathbf{1}(\hat{a}\in{\mathcal{A}}){\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},\hat{a})\rVert^{2}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ax1.E9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ax1.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle={\mathbb{E}}_{p({\bm{x}},a)}\sum_{\hat{a}\in\hat{\mathcal{A}}}q^{*}(\hat{a}\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a))\lVert{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a)-\mathbf{1}(\hat{a}\in{\mathcal{A}}){\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},\hat{a})\rVert^{2}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝒈</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒈</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒈</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle={\mathbb{E}}_{p({\bm{x}},a)}\sum_{\hat{a}\in\hat{\mathcal{A}}}q^{*}(\hat{a}\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a))\lVert{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a)-\mathbf{1}(\hat{a}\in{\mathcal{A}}){\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},\hat{a})\rVert^{2}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ax1.E10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ax1.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle={\mathbb{E}}_{p({\bm{x}},a)}\sum_{\hat{a}\in\hat{\mathcal{A}}}\mathbf{1}(\hat{a}=a)\lVert{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a)-\mathbf{1}(\hat{a}\in{\mathcal{A}}){\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},\hat{a})\rVert^{2}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒈</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒈</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle={\mathbb{E}}_{p({\bm{x}},a)}\sum_{\hat{a}\in\hat{\mathcal{A}}}\mathbf{1}(\hat{a}=a)\lVert{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a)-\mathbf{1}(\hat{a}\in{\mathcal{A}}){\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},\hat{a})\rVert^{2}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ax1.E11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ax1.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle={\mathbb{E}}_{p({\bm{x}},a)}\lVert{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a)-\mathbf{1}(a\in{\mathcal{A}}){\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a)\rVert^{2}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒈</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒈</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle={\mathbb{E}}_{p({\bm{x}},a)}\lVert{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a)-\mathbf{1}(a\in{\mathcal{A}}){\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a)\rVert^{2}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ax1.E12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ax1.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle={\mathbb{E}}_{p({\bm{x}},a)}\lVert{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a)-{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a)\rVert^{2}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒈</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝒈</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle={\mathbb{E}}_{p({\bm{x}},a)}\lVert{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a)-{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a)\rVert^{2}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ax1.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ax1.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle={\mathbb{E}}_{p({\bm{x}},a)}0=0\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle={\mathbb{E}}_{p({\bm{x}},a)}0=0\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ax1.p19.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax1.p19.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the fourth equality used the fact that <math id="Ax1.p19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{A}}\subseteq\hat{\mathcal{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{A}}\subseteq\hat{\mathcal{A}}</annotation></semantics></math>, which holds since <math id="Ax1.p19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{k}\geq k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>≥</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{k}\geq k</annotation></semantics></math>. This concludes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Ax1.p20" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.p20.1" class="ltx_p">The following lemma simply states that if the integral of a non-negative continuous function <math id="Ax1.p20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> w.r.t. to some measure <math id="Ax1.p20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> is equal to zero, then the function must be zero on the support of <math id="Ax1.p20.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 5</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X,\tau)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X,\tau)</annotation></semantics></math> be a topological space and let <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> be the Borel sigma-algebra for <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu:{\mathcal{F}}\rightarrow[0,\infty)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu:{\mathcal{F}}\rightarrow[0,\infty)</annotation></semantics></math> be a measure and let <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:X\rightarrow[0,\infty)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:X\rightarrow[0,\infty)</annotation></semantics></math> be a non-negative continuous function. If <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int fd\mu=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int fd\mu=0</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(x)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x)=0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\textnormal{supp}[\mu]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mtext>supp</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\textnormal{supp}[\mu]</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Ax1.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="Ax1.p21" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.p21.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax1.p21.1.1" class="ltx_text">We show the contrapositive statement. Suppose there exists <math id="Ax1.p21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}\in\textnormal{supp}[\mu]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mtext>supp</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}\in\textnormal{supp}[\mu]</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="Ax1.p21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(x_{0})&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x_{0})&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="Ax1.p21.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is continuous, we have that <math id="Ax1.p21.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{-1}((0,\infty))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>,</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{-1}((0,\infty))</annotation></semantics></math> is an open neighborhood of <math id="Ax1.p21.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="Ax1.p21.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}\in\textnormal{supp}[\mu]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mtext>supp</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}\in\textnormal{supp}[\mu]</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that <math id="Ax1.p21.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu(f^{-1}((0,\infty)))&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu(f^{-1}((0,\infty)))&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. But this means <math id="Ax1.p21.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int fd\mu&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int fd\mu&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx1" title="" class="ltx_ref">1</a>, Section 3A, Exercise 3]</cite>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Ax1.p22" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.p22.1" class="ltx_p">We are finally ready to prove <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ 2.5 Main identifiability result ‣ 2 Identifiability analysis of LAPO ‣ On the Identifiability of Latent Action Policies" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Ax1.p23" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.p23.1" class="ltx_p">See <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ 2.5 Main identifiability result ‣ 2 Identifiability analysis of LAPO ‣ On the Identifiability of Latent Action Policies" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></p>
</div>
<div id="Ax1.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="Ax1.p24" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.p24.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax1.p24.1.1" class="ltx_text">If <math id="Ax1.p24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\hat{\bm{g}},\hat{q})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒈</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\hat{\bm{g}},\hat{q})</annotation></semantics></math> solves Problem <a href="#S2.E1" title="In 2.3 A formal entropy-regularized LAPO objective ‣ 2 Identifiability analysis of LAPO ‣ On the Identifiability of Latent Action Policies" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, we must have <math id="Ax1.p24.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\bm{g}}\in{\mathcal{G}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒈</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\bm{g}}\in{\mathcal{G}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Ax1.p24.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{q}\in{\mathcal{Q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{q}\in{\mathcal{Q}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, since <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1 (Continuous 𝒈). ‣ 2.5 Main identifiability result ‣ 2 Identifiability analysis of LAPO ‣ On the Identifiability of Latent Action Policies" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Assumptions</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and <a href="#Thmassumption2" title="Assumption 2 (Injectivity). ‣ 2.5 Main identifiability result ‣ 2 Identifiability analysis of LAPO ‣ On the Identifiability of Latent Action Policies" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> hold and <math id="Ax1.p24.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{k}\geq k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>≥</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{k}\geq k</annotation></semantics></math>, we can apply <a href="#Thmtheorem4" title="Proposition 4. ‣ Appendix ‣ On the Identifiability of Latent Action Policies" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> to conclude that there exists a pair <math id="Ax1.p24.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\bm{g}}^{*},q^{*})\in{\mathcal{G}}\times{\mathcal{Q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒈</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\bm{g}}^{*},q^{*})\in{\mathcal{G}}\times{\mathcal{Q}}</annotation></semantics></math> that reaches zero loss. From this, we conclude that <math id="Ax1.p24.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\hat{\bm{g}},\hat{q})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒈</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\hat{\bm{g}},\hat{q})</annotation></semantics></math> must also reach zero loss, otherwise it is not optimal.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Ax1.p25" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.p25.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax1.p25.1.1" class="ltx_text">Thus we have</span></p>
<table id="Ax1.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Ax1.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ax1.E14.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathbb{E}}_{p({\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})}\left[\sum_{\hat{a}\in\hat{\mathcal{A}}}\hat{q}(\hat{a}\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})\lVert{\bm{x}}^{\prime}-\hat{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},\hat{a})\rVert^{2}_{2}+H(\hat{q}(\cdot\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime}))\right]=0\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></munder></mstyle><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒈</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathbb{E}}_{p({\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})}\left[\sum_{\hat{a}\in\hat{\mathcal{A}}}\hat{q}(\hat{a}\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})\lVert{\bm{x}}^{\prime}-\hat{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},\hat{a})\rVert^{2}_{2}+H(\hat{q}(\cdot\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime}))\right]=0\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ax1.p25.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax1.p25.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since both terms are lower bounded by 0, both terms must equal zero. We start by using the fact that the entropy term is equal to zero:</span></p>
<table id="Ax1.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Ax1.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ax1.E15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathbb{E}}_{p({\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})}H(\hat{q}(\cdot\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathbb{E}}_{p({\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})}H(\hat{q}(\cdot\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ax1.E15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ax1.E16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ax1.E16.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathbb{E}}_{p({\bm{x}},a)}H(\hat{q}(\cdot\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a)))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒈</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathbb{E}}_{p({\bm{x}},a)}H(\hat{q}(\cdot\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a)))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ax1.E16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ax1.E17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ax1.E17.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathbb{E}}_{p(a)}{\mathbb{E}}_{p({\bm{x}}\mid a)}H(\hat{q}(\cdot\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a)))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒈</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathbb{E}}_{p(a)}{\mathbb{E}}_{p({\bm{x}}\mid a)}H(\hat{q}(\cdot\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a)))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ax1.E17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ax1.E18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ax1.E18.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{a\in\textnormal{supp}[p(a)]}p(a){\mathbb{E}}_{p({\bm{x}}\mid a)}H(\hat{q}(\cdot\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a)))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mtext>supp</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒈</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{a\in\textnormal{supp}[p(a)]}p(a){\mathbb{E}}_{p({\bm{x}}\mid a)}H(\hat{q}(\cdot\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a)))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ax1.E18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=0\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=0\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ax1.p25.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax1.p25.3.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="Ax1.p25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p({\bm{x}},a):=p({\bm{x}})\pi(a\mid{\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p({\bm{x}},a):=p({\bm{x}})\pi(a\mid{\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Ax1.p25.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(a):=\int p({\bm{x}},a)d{\bm{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(a):=\int p({\bm{x}},a)d{\bm{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Ax1.p25.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p({\bm{x}}\mid a):=p({\bm{x}},a)/p(a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p({\bm{x}}\mid a):=p({\bm{x}},a)/p(a)</annotation></semantics></math>. The l.h.s. is a sum of positive terms. We thus have, for each <math id="Ax1.p25.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in\textnormal{supp}[p(a)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mtext>supp</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in\textnormal{supp}[p(a)]</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="Ax1.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Ax1.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ax1.E19.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathbb{E}}_{p({\bm{x}}\mid a)}H(\hat{q}(\cdot\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a)))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒈</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathbb{E}}_{p({\bm{x}}\mid a)}H(\hat{q}(\cdot\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a)))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ax1.E19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=0\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=0\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ax1.p25.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax1.p25.4.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="Ax1.p25.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="H(\hat{q}(\cdot\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a)))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒈</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(\hat{q}(\cdot\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a)))</annotation></semantics></math> is greater or equal to zero and is a continuous function of <math id="Ax1.p25.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒙</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> (it follows from the continuity of <math id="Ax1.p25.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒈</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Ax1.p25.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{q}(\hat{a}\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{q}(\hat{a}\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Ax1.p25.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\mapsto y\log y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\mapsto y\log y</annotation></semantics></math><span id="footnote5" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">5</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">5</sup>
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">5</span>
                
                
                
                
                
                
                
              In the definition of entropy, <math id="footnote5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\log 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\log 0</annotation></semantics></math> is defined to be equal to zero, which makes <math id="footnote5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\mapsto y\log y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\mapsto y\log y</annotation></semantics></math> a continuous function on <math id="footnote5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,\infty)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,\infty)</annotation></semantics></math> since <math id="footnote5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{y\to 0^{+}}y\log y=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{y\to 0^{+}}y\log y=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span></span>), <a href="#Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma 5. ‣ Appendix ‣ On the Identifiability of Latent Action Policies" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> implies that <math id="Ax1.p25.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="H(\hat{q}(\cdot\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a)))=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒈</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(\hat{q}(\cdot\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a)))=0</annotation></semantics></math>, for all <math id="Ax1.p25.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}\in\textnormal{supp}[p({\bm{x}}\mid a)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mtext>supp</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}\in\textnormal{supp}[p({\bm{x}}\mid a)]</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Ax1.p26" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.p26.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax1.p26.1.1" class="ltx_text">To summarize, we showed that, for all <math id="Ax1.p26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in\textnormal{supp}[p(a)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mtext>supp</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in\textnormal{supp}[p(a)]</annotation></semantics></math> and all <math id="Ax1.p26.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}\in\textnormal{supp}[p({\bm{x}}\mid a)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mtext>supp</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}\in\textnormal{supp}[p({\bm{x}}\mid a)]</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that <math id="Ax1.p26.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{H(\hat{q}(\cdot\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a)))=0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒈</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{H(\hat{q}(\cdot\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a)))=0}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since</span></p>
<table id="Ax1.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ax1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigcup_{a\in\textnormal{supp}[p(a)]}\textnormal{supp}[p({\bm{x}}\mid a)]\times\{a\}=\textnormal{supp}[p({\bm{x}},a)]\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">⋃</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mtext>supp</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mtext>supp</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>supp</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigcup_{a\in\textnormal{supp}[p(a)]}\textnormal{supp}[p({\bm{x}}\mid a)]\times\{a\}=\textnormal{supp}[p({\bm{x}},a)]\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ax1.p26.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax1.p26.2.1" class="ltx_text">it is equivalent to saying that, for all <math id="Ax1.p26.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\bm{x}},a)\in\textnormal{supp}[p({\bm{x}},a)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mtext>supp</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\bm{x}},a)\in\textnormal{supp}[p({\bm{x}},a)]</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="Ax1.p26.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{H(\hat{q}(\cdot\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a)))=0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒈</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{H(\hat{q}(\cdot\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a)))=0}</annotation></semantics></math>. This means there exists a function <math id="Ax1.p26.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{v}}:\textnormal{supp}[p({\bm{x}},a)]\rightarrow\hat{\mathcal{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒗</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>supp</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{v}}:\textnormal{supp}[p({\bm{x}},a)]\rightarrow\hat{\mathcal{A}}</annotation></semantics></math> such that, for all <math id="Ax1.p26.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\bm{x}},a)\in\textnormal{supp}[p({\bm{x}},a)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mtext>supp</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\bm{x}},a)\in\textnormal{supp}[p({\bm{x}},a)]</annotation></semantics></math> and all <math id="Ax1.p26.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{a}\in\hat{\mathcal{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{a}\in\hat{\mathcal{A}}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="Ax1.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Ax1.E20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ax1.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{q}(\hat{a}\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a))=\mathbf{1}(\hat{a}={\bm{v}}({\bm{x}},a))\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝒈</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{q}(\hat{a}\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a))=\mathbf{1}(\hat{a}={\bm{v}}({\bm{x}},a))\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ax1.p26.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax1.p26.3.1" class="ltx_text">which proves the first statement.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Ax1.p27" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.p27.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax1.p27.1.1" class="ltx_text">To prove the second statement, we rewrite the above equation as</span></p>
<table id="Ax1.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Ax1.E21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ax1.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{q}(\hat{a}\mid G({\bm{x}},a))=\mathbf{1}(\hat{a}={\bm{v}}({\bm{x}},a))\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{q}(\hat{a}\mid G({\bm{x}},a))=\mathbf{1}(\hat{a}={\bm{v}}({\bm{x}},a))\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ax1.p27.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax1.p27.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="Ax1.p27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G:{\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{A}}\rightarrow{\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{X}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G:{\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{A}}\rightarrow{\mathcal{X}}\times{\mathcal{X}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> was previously defined as <math id="Ax1.p27.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G({\bm{x}},a):=({\bm{x}},{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝒈</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G({\bm{x}},a):=({\bm{x}},{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a))</annotation></semantics></math>. For each pair <math id="Ax1.p27.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a,\hat{a})\in{\mathcal{A}}\times\hat{\mathcal{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a,\hat{a})\in{\mathcal{A}}\times\hat{\mathcal{A}}</annotation></semantics></math>, define the function <math id="Ax1.p27.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{q}_{a,\hat{a}}:{\mathcal{X}}\rightarrow[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{q}_{a,\hat{a}}:{\mathcal{X}}\rightarrow[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="Ax1.p27.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{q}_{a,\hat{a}}({\bm{x}}):=\hat{q}(\hat{a}\mid G({\bm{x}},a))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{q}_{a,\hat{a}}({\bm{x}}):=\hat{q}(\hat{a}\mid G({\bm{x}},a))</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="Ax1.p27.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{q}_{a,\hat{a}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{q}_{a,\hat{a}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the composition of two continuous functions, namely <math id="Ax1.p27.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G(\cdot,a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G(\cdot,a)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Ax1.p27.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\hat{q}(\hat{a}\mid\cdot,\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{q}(\hat{a}\mid\cdot,\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>, it must also be continuous. We rewrite <a href="#Ax1.E21" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix ‣ On the Identifiability of Latent Action Policies" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a> as follows: for all <math id="Ax1.p27.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{a}\in\hat{\mathcal{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{a}\in\hat{\mathcal{A}}</annotation></semantics></math>, all <math id="Ax1.p27.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in\textnormal{supp}[p(a)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mtext>supp</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in\textnormal{supp}[p(a)]</annotation></semantics></math> and all <math id="Ax1.p27.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}\in\textnormal{supp}[p({\bm{x}}\mid a)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mtext>supp</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}\in\textnormal{supp}[p({\bm{x}}\mid a)]</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="Ax1.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Ax1.E22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ax1.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{q}_{a,\hat{a}}({\bm{x}})=\mathbf{1}(\hat{a}={\bm{v}}({\bm{x}},a))\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{q}_{a,\hat{a}}({\bm{x}})=\mathbf{1}(\hat{a}={\bm{v}}({\bm{x}},a))\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ax1.p27.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax1.p27.3.1" class="ltx_text">Now, fix <math id="Ax1.p27.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{a}\in\hat{\mathcal{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{a}\in\hat{\mathcal{A}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Ax1.p27.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in\textnormal{supp}[p(a)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mtext>supp</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in\textnormal{supp}[p(a)]</annotation></semantics></math>. It is clear from the above equation that <math id="Ax1.p27.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{q}_{a,\hat{a}}(\textnormal{supp}[p({\bm{x}}\mid a)])\subseteq\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>supp</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{q}_{a,\hat{a}}(\textnormal{supp}[p({\bm{x}}\mid a)])\subseteq\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math>. But since <math id="Ax1.p27.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textnormal{supp}[p({\bm{x}}\mid a)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>supp</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textnormal{supp}[p({\bm{x}}\mid a)]</annotation></semantics></math> is connected (<a href="#Thmassumption3" title="Assumption 3. ‣ 2.5 Main identifiability result ‣ 2 Identifiability analysis of LAPO ‣ On the Identifiability of Latent Action Policies" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Assumption</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>) and <math id="Ax1.p27.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{q}_{a,\hat{a}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{q}_{a,\hat{a}}</annotation></semantics></math> is continuous, we know that the image <math id="Ax1.p27.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{q}_{a,\hat{a}}(\textnormal{supp}[p({\bm{x}}\mid a)])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>supp</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{q}_{a,\hat{a}}(\textnormal{supp}[p({\bm{x}}\mid a)])</annotation></semantics></math> must also be connected. This implies that <math id="Ax1.p27.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{q}_{a,\hat{a}}(\textnormal{supp}[p({\bm{x}}\mid a)])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>supp</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{q}_{a,\hat{a}}(\textnormal{supp}[p({\bm{x}}\mid a)])</annotation></semantics></math> is either <math id="Ax1.p27.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{0\}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="Ax1.p27.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{1\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, there is a function <math id="Ax1.p27.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi:\textnormal{supp}[p(a)]\times\hat{\mathcal{A}}\rightarrow\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>supp</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi:\textnormal{supp}[p(a)]\times\hat{\mathcal{A}}\rightarrow\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math> that outputs the value that <math id="Ax1.p27.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{q}_{a,\hat{a}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{q}_{a,\hat{a}}</annotation></semantics></math> uniformly takes on <math id="Ax1.p27.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textnormal{supp}[p({\bm{x}}\mid a)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>supp</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textnormal{supp}[p({\bm{x}}\mid a)]</annotation></semantics></math>. In other words, for all <math id="Ax1.p27.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{a}\in\hat{\mathcal{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{a}\in\hat{\mathcal{A}}</annotation></semantics></math>, all <math id="Ax1.p27.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in\textnormal{supp}[p(a)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mtext>supp</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in\textnormal{supp}[p(a)]</annotation></semantics></math> and all <math id="Ax1.p27.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}\in\textnormal{supp}[p({\bm{x}}\mid a)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mtext>supp</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}\in\textnormal{supp}[p({\bm{x}}\mid a)]</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="Ax1.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Ax1.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ax1.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{q}_{a,\hat{a}}({\bm{x}})=\phi(a,\hat{a})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{q}_{a,\hat{a}}({\bm{x}})=\phi(a,\hat{a})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ax1.E24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ax1.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{1}(\hat{a}={\bm{v}}({\bm{x}},a))=\phi(a,\hat{a})\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{1}(\hat{a}={\bm{v}}({\bm{x}},a))=\phi(a,\hat{a})\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ax1.p27.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax1.p27.4.1" class="ltx_text">The last equation above implies that <math id="Ax1.p27.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{v}}({\bm{x}},a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{v}}({\bm{x}},a)</annotation></semantics></math> is constant in <math id="Ax1.p27.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒙</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}</annotation></semantics></math>, for all values of <math id="Ax1.p27.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in\textnormal{supp}[p(a)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mtext>supp</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in\textnormal{supp}[p(a)]</annotation></semantics></math>. This means there is a function <math id="Ax1.p27.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{v}}:\textnormal{supp}[p(a)]\rightarrow\hat{\mathcal{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒗</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>supp</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{v}}:\textnormal{supp}[p(a)]\rightarrow\hat{\mathcal{A}}</annotation></semantics></math> such that, for all <math id="Ax1.p27.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in\textnormal{supp}[p(a)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mtext>supp</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in\textnormal{supp}[p(a)]</annotation></semantics></math> and all <math id="Ax1.p27.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}\in\textnormal{supp}[p({\bm{x}}\mid a)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mtext>supp</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}\in\textnormal{supp}[p({\bm{x}}\mid a)]</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="Ax1.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Ax1.E25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ax1.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\bm{v}}({\bm{x}},a)={\bm{v}}(a)\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\bm{v}}({\bm{x}},a)={\bm{v}}(a)\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ax1.p27.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax1.p27.5.1" class="ltx_text">which shows the second statement.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Ax1.p28" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.p28.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax1.p28.1.1" class="ltx_text">To prove the third statement (<math id="Ax1.p28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{v}}(a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{v}}(a)</annotation></semantics></math> injective), we leverage the fact that the reconstruction term is equal to zero:</span></p>
<table id="Ax1.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Ax1.E26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ax1.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathbb{E}}_{p({\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})}\sum_{\hat{a}\in\hat{\mathcal{A}}}\hat{q}(\hat{a}\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})\lVert{\bm{x}}^{\prime}-\hat{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},\hat{a})\rVert^{2}_{2}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒈</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathbb{E}}_{p({\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})}\sum_{\hat{a}\in\hat{\mathcal{A}}}\hat{q}(\hat{a}\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{x}}^{\prime})\lVert{\bm{x}}^{\prime}-\hat{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},\hat{a})\rVert^{2}_{2}=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ax1.E27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ax1.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathbb{E}}_{p({\bm{x}},a)}\sum_{\hat{a}\in\hat{\mathcal{A}}}\hat{q}(\hat{a}\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a))\lVert{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a)-\hat{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},\hat{a})\rVert^{2}_{2}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝒈</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒈</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒈</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathbb{E}}_{p({\bm{x}},a)}\sum_{\hat{a}\in\hat{\mathcal{A}}}\hat{q}(\hat{a}\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a))\lVert{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a)-\hat{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},\hat{a})\rVert^{2}_{2}=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ax1.E28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ax1.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathbb{E}}_{p(a)}{\mathbb{E}}_{p({\bm{x}}\mid a)}\sum_{\hat{a}\in\hat{\mathcal{A}}}\hat{q}(\hat{a}\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a))\lVert{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a)-\hat{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},\hat{a})\rVert^{2}_{2}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝒈</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒈</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒈</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathbb{E}}_{p(a)}{\mathbb{E}}_{p({\bm{x}}\mid a)}\sum_{\hat{a}\in\hat{\mathcal{A}}}\hat{q}(\hat{a}\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a))\lVert{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a)-\hat{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},\hat{a})\rVert^{2}_{2}=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ax1.p28.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax1.p28.2.1" class="ltx_text">The term inside the expectation <math id="Ax1.p28.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{E}}_{p(a)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{E}}_{p(a)}</annotation></semantics></math> are greater or equal to zero, thus each of them must be equal to zero, i.e. for all <math id="Ax1.p28.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in\textnormal{supp}[p(a)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mtext>supp</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in\textnormal{supp}[p(a)]</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="Ax1.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Ax1.E30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ax1.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathbb{E}}_{p({\bm{x}}\mid a)}\sum_{\hat{a}\in\hat{\mathcal{A}}}\hat{q}(\hat{a}\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a))\lVert{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a)-\hat{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},\hat{a})\rVert^{2}_{2}=0\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝒈</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒈</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒈</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathbb{E}}_{p({\bm{x}}\mid a)}\sum_{\hat{a}\in\hat{\mathcal{A}}}\hat{q}(\hat{a}\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a))\lVert{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a)-\hat{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},\hat{a})\rVert^{2}_{2}=0\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ax1.p28.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax1.p28.3.1" class="ltx_text">Since the inside of the expectation is always greater or equal to zero and is a continuous function of <math id="Ax1.p28.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒙</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <a href="#Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma 5. ‣ Appendix ‣ On the Identifiability of Latent Action Policies" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> implies that, for all <math id="Ax1.p28.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}\in\textnormal{supp}[p({\bm{x}}\mid a)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mtext>supp</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}\in\textnormal{supp}[p({\bm{x}}\mid a)]</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
<table id="Ax1.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Ax1.E31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ax1.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{\hat{a}\in\hat{\mathcal{A}}}\hat{q}(\hat{a}\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a))\lVert{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a)-\hat{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},\hat{a})\rVert^{2}_{2}=0\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝒈</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒈</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒈</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{\hat{a}\in\hat{\mathcal{A}}}\hat{q}(\hat{a}\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a))\lVert{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a)-\hat{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},\hat{a})\rVert^{2}_{2}=0\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ax1.p28.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax1.p28.4.1" class="ltx_text">To summarize, we showed that, for all <math id="Ax1.p28.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in\textnormal{supp}[p(a)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mtext>supp</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in\textnormal{supp}[p(a)]</annotation></semantics></math> and all <math id="Ax1.p28.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}\in\textnormal{supp}[p({\bm{x}}\mid a)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mtext>supp</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}\in\textnormal{supp}[p({\bm{x}}\mid a)]</annotation></semantics></math>, <a href="#Ax1.E31" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix ‣ On the Identifiability of Latent Action Policies" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">31</span></a> holds. We can thus derive that</span></p>
<table id="Ax1.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Ax1.E32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ax1.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 0=\sum_{\hat{a}\in\hat{\mathcal{A}}}\hat{q}(\hat{a}\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a))\lVert{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a)-\hat{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},\hat{a})\rVert^{2}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝒈</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒈</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒈</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 0=\sum_{\hat{a}\in\hat{\mathcal{A}}}\hat{q}(\hat{a}\mid{\bm{x}},{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a))\lVert{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a)-\hat{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},\hat{a})\rVert^{2}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ax1.E32.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{\hat{a}\in\hat{\mathcal{A}}}\mathbf{1}(\hat{a}={\bm{v}}({\bm{x}},a))\lVert{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a)-\hat{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},\hat{a})\rVert^{2}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒈</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒈</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{\hat{a}\in\hat{\mathcal{A}}}\mathbf{1}(\hat{a}={\bm{v}}({\bm{x}},a))\lVert{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a)-\hat{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},\hat{a})\rVert^{2}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ax1.E33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ax1.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{\hat{a}\in\hat{\mathcal{A}}}\mathbf{1}(\hat{a}={\bm{v}}(a))\lVert{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a)-\hat{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},\hat{a})\rVert^{2}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒈</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒈</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{\hat{a}\in\hat{\mathcal{A}}}\mathbf{1}(\hat{a}={\bm{v}}(a))\lVert{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a)-\hat{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},\hat{a})\rVert^{2}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ax1.E34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ax1.E34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\lVert{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a)-\hat{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},{\bm{v}}(a))\rVert^{2}_{2}\," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒈</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒈</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\lVert{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a)-\hat{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},{\bm{v}}(a))\rVert^{2}_{2}\,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ax1.p28.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax1.p28.5.1" class="ltx_text">where the first line leverages <a href="#Ax1.E20" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix ‣ On the Identifiability of Latent Action Policies" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a> and the second line uses <a href="#Ax1.E25" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix ‣ On the Identifiability of Latent Action Policies" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">25</span></a>.
This means that, for all <math id="Ax1.p28.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in\textnormal{supp}[p(a)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mtext>supp</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in\textnormal{supp}[p(a)]</annotation></semantics></math> and all <math id="Ax1.p28.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}\in\textnormal{supp}[p({\bm{x}}\mid a)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mtext>supp</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}\in\textnormal{supp}[p({\bm{x}}\mid a)]</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="Ax1.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Ax1.E35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ax1.E35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a)=\hat{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},{\bm{v}}(a))\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒈</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒈</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝒗</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},a)=\hat{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}},{\bm{v}}(a))\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ax1.p28.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax1.p28.6.1" class="ltx_text">We now show that <math id="Ax1.p28.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{v}}:\textnormal{supp}[p(a)]\rightarrow\hat{\mathcal{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒗</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>supp</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{v}}:\textnormal{supp}[p(a)]\rightarrow\hat{\mathcal{A}}</annotation></semantics></math> is injective. We proceed by contradiction. Suppose it is not injective. This means there exist two distinct <math id="Ax1.p28.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{1},a_{2}\in\textnormal{supp}[p(a)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mtext>supp</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1},a_{2}\in\textnormal{supp}[p(a)]</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="Ax1.p28.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{v}}(a_{1})={\bm{v}}(a_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{v}}(a_{1})={\bm{v}}(a_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>. By <a href="#Thmassumption4" title="Assumption 4. ‣ 2.5 Main identifiability result ‣ 2 Identifiability analysis of LAPO ‣ On the Identifiability of Latent Action Policies" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Assumption</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, we know there exists an <math id="Ax1.p28.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> that is in both <math id="Ax1.p28.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textnormal{supp}[p({\bm{x}}\mid a_{1})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>supp</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textnormal{supp}[p({\bm{x}}\mid a_{1})]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Ax1.p28.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textnormal{supp}[p({\bm{x}}\mid a_{2})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>supp</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textnormal{supp}[p({\bm{x}}\mid a_{2})]</annotation></semantics></math>. We note that</span></p>
<table id="Ax1.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Ax1.E36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ax1.E36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}}_{0},a_{1})=\hat{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}}_{0},{\bm{v}}(a_{1}))=\hat{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}}_{0},{\bm{v}}(a_{2}))={\bm{g}}({\bm{x}}_{0},a_{2})\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒈</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒈</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒈</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝒈</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}}_{0},a_{1})=\hat{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}}_{0},{\bm{v}}(a_{1}))=\hat{\bm{g}}({\bm{x}}_{0},{\bm{v}}(a_{2}))={\bm{g}}({\bm{x}}_{0},a_{2})\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ax1.p28.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax1.p28.7.1" class="ltx_text">where the first equality holds because <math id="Ax1.p28.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{0}\in\textnormal{supp}[p({\bm{x}}\mid a_{1})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mtext>supp</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{0}\in\textnormal{supp}[p({\bm{x}}\mid a_{1})]</annotation></semantics></math> and the last equality holds because <math id="Ax1.p28.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{0}\in\textnormal{supp}[p({\bm{x}}\mid a_{2})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mtext>supp</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{0}\in\textnormal{supp}[p({\bm{x}}\mid a_{2})]</annotation></semantics></math>. But this is contradicting <a href="#Thmassumption2" title="Assumption 2 (Injectivity). ‣ 2.5 Main identifiability result ‣ 2 Identifiability analysis of LAPO ‣ On the Identifiability of Latent Action Policies" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Assumption</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. Thus, <math id="Ax1.p28.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{v}}(a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{v}}(a)</annotation></semantics></math> is injective.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
